  'keyword.title':       'Keyword Monitoring',
  'keyword.subtitle':    'Monitor the presence/absence of a keyword in web pages (case-insensitive).',
  'keyword.how1': 'A direct GET from the monitoring server (single pod); redirects are followed and SSL verification is OFF (internal-CA/self-signed pages work too — certificate validity is a separate monitor type). The body is read but capped at ~2 MB (memory guard). 443 is not required; the scheme depends on the monitor URL. No proxy is used.',
  'keyword.how2': 'The keyword is searched in the body; case-insensitive by default (case-sensitive via a toggle). The present/absent condition and count threshold (≥, ≤, =, >, <) are applied by the scheduler. Result: found or not, count, status code, response time, short snippet.',
  'keyword.how3': 'Cache-busting: {timestamp} in the URL is replaced with the current Unix second each run; custom headers (e.g. Cache-Control: no-cache) can also be added. An SSRF guard runs before the request.',
