  'ping.title':       'Ping Monitoring',
  'ping.subtitle':    'Continuously monitor your hosts with ICMP ping; alert when unreachable.',
  'ping.how1': 'Not Java ICMP — from the monitoring server (single pod) the OS "ping" command is run as a short-lived subprocess (real ICMP echo, direct). On Linux ping -c <count> -w <seconds>; packet-loss % and average RTT are parsed from the output. IP version (v4/v6) is selectable.',
  'ping.how2': 'Result: reachable or not (packet loss below 100% or an RTT was measured), RTT (ms) and packet-loss percentage.',
  'ping.how3': 'Environment caveat: in a locked-down pod without sufficient privilege (CAP_NET_RAW / net.ipv4.ping_group_range), on a "permission denied" output the check degrades to N/A instead of failing ("ICMP not available in this environment"). There is no TCP fallback.',
