  'port.title':           'Port Monitoring',
  'port.subtitle':        'Useful for SMTP, POP3, FTP and other services running on specific TCP ports.',
  'port.how1': 'A direct connection from the monitoring server (single pod); by protocol: TCP = raw socket connect (is the port open), TLS = TCP + SNI handshake (does the server present a certificate), HTTP = status-code check, BANNER = connect and match the response banner against the "expected" text, UDP = send a datagram and interpret reply/unreachable/timeout (less reliable since it is connectionless). No proxy is used.',
  'port.how2': 'Timeout defaults to 5s. Configurable: expected response text (expect), data to send (sendData), IP version (auto/v4/v6). Result: open/closed + response time.',
  'port.how3': 'SSRF guard: connects only to validated IPs (DNS-rebind closed). For multi-A hosts the first accepting IP is chosen (avoids a false "refused" from a split VIP).',
